## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design content-based routing, with strict per-record validation and multi-stream fan-out. Emphasizes end-to-end tracing, fault handling, and test strategy in a realistic, beginner-friendly context.

## Key Concepts
- Content-based routing with multiple Kinesis streams
- Lambda validation of JSON schema and required fields
- Per-record tracing with AWS X-Ray
- Parquet writing to S3 and DLQ for invalid data
- LocalStack end-to-end testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-validator outline
function validate(record) {
  const hasFields = record.deviceId && record.ts && record.correlationId && typeof record.severity === 'number';
  const okSeverity = record.severity >= 0 && record.severity <= 100;
  return hasFields && okSeverity;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle backpressure if one stream lags significantly?
- What metrics would you emit to monitor data quality and latency?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of enterprise-scale data pipeline challenges including multi-region architecture, schema evolution management, data governance compliance, automated recovery mechanisms, and observability patterns in production environments.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region data residency enforcement with tenant isolation
- Schema evolution and drift detection at ingestion boundaries
- Quarantine workflows for non-conforming data preservation
- SLA-driven automated backfill with replay mechanisms
- Distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry across regional boundaries
- Idempotent processing patterns and cost-optimized resource allocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Schema validation with tenant awareness
function validateRecord(record, tenantSchema) {
  if (record.schemaVersion !== tenantSchema.version) {
    return { valid: false, reason: 'schema_version_mismatch' };
  }

  const requiredFields = tenantSchema.fields.filter(f => f.required);
  const missingFields = requiredFields.filter(f => !(f.name in record));

  return missingFields.length === 0 
    ? { valid: true } 
    : { valid: false, reason: 'missing_fields', fields: missingFields };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end multi-tenant design, runtime feature toggles, schema evolution, and deterministic replay using AWS DVA primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation with Lake Formation and tenant-scoped keys
- Schema evolution via Glue Schema Registry with backward/forward compatibility
- Deterministic replay using per-tenant replay token in DynamoDB
- Idempotent writes by deduping event_id in DynamoDB
- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry; secure access controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo dedupe and write path
async function processEvent(evt){
  const {tenant_id, event_id, payload} = evt;
  // ensure idempotent dedupe
  const exists = await dynamo.get({TableName:'TenantDedup', Key:{tenant_id, event_id}});
  if (exists.Item) return;
  await dynamo.put({TableName:'TenantDedup', Item:{tenant_id, event_id, ts: Date.now()}});
  // write raw to S3 with partition tenant/date (implementation omitted)
}
```

